repository-code: "https://github.com/impala9397-hub/programmable-medicine-target-discriminator-atlas"
abstract: >-
  A logic-gating target-discovery pipeline for triple-negative breast cancer.
  Cell-surface proteins and extracellular proteases are scored on independent
  axes — organ specificity, interpatient coverage, and intratumoral coverage —
  and then composed into 2-to-3-input Boolean gates of the form
  (A OR B) AND protease, which widen malignant-cell coverage with an OR while a
  protease AND restores organ specificity. The recommended discriminator is
  (EPCAM OR VTCN1) AND MMP11. The logic is modality-independent and can be
  realized as a logic-gated CAR-T cell or as a protease-activated pro-antibody.
keywords:
  - target discovery
  - logic gating
  - synthetic biology
  - CAR-T
  - triple-negative breast cancer
  - surfaceome
  - protease
  - single-cell
